==The Sims 2==
{{Main|List of songs in The Sims 2}}
''The Sims 2'' soundtrack music was set up by [[Maxis|Maxis']] audio director Robi Kauker, with composers like The Humble Brothers or John Cobbett. The music took about a year to record and was restricted from being repetitive. Kauker says, "Diehard Sim fans spend virtual lifetimes playing, so the music can't be repetitive."<ref name="gs">[http://www.gamespot.com/pc/strategy/thesims2/news.html?sid=6119747 Spot On: Simlish stylist Robi Kauker] at GameSpot.</ref>

The theme music and music from the [[Create a Sim|Create-A-Sim]] portion of the game was created by Mark Mothersbaugh, a founding member of Devo, whom Maxis enlisted.<ref name="gs" />

Music from ''[[The Sims 2]]'' and ''[[The Sims 2: University]]'' was remixed by real DJs in ''[[The Sims 2: Nightlife]]''.<ref name="gs" />

